{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--sakhalin-greeting-irankarahtee-universal","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--greetings"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, the greeting 'irankarahtee can be used at any time of day, anywhere, regardless of the addressee.","ja":"樺太アイヌにおいて、挨拶表現 'irankarahtee は時間・場所・相手を問わず使用できる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["'irankarahtee"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0016-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--interjection-morphology-i-verb-causative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--greetings"],"statement":{"en":"Many interjections have the morphological structure i- + intransitive verb stem + causative suffix.","ja":"多くの間投詞は i- + 自動詞語幹 + 使役接尾辞という形態構造を持つ。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"major","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["irayapka","iyairaykere","iyaykipte","i-","-re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0289-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--i-causative-interjections-lack-verbal-use","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--greetings"],"statement":{"en":"Interjections with the shape i- + verb + causative suffix are normally not used as verbs in that form, verbal use being restricted to the base stem.","ja":"i- + 動詞 + 使役接尾辞の構成を持つ間投詞はその形のまま動詞として用いられることは通例なく、動詞としては基底の語幹形のみが用いられる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"major","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["iyairaykere","yairayke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0289-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--shizunai-iyayraykere-etymology-and-function","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--greetings"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai, iyayraykere is a formal expression of gratitude literally meaning 'it makes me kill myself'.","ja":"静内方言において、iyayraykere は改まった感謝表現であり、字義通りには「それは私に自死させる」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["iyayraykere"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0126-03","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0127-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"supports","claim":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--interjection-morphology-i-verb-causative","differs_in":null,"note":"Refsing's literal analysis of iyayraykere matches Nakagawa's productive i- + intransitive + causative template."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--onomatopoeic-roots-inventory-chiri","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--ideophones"],"statement":{"en":"The forms hum, kit, pat, put, rim, and shiu, as well as mai, nai, and ser in -kosanu derivatives, are onomatopoeic roots.","ja":"hum、kit、pat、put、rim、shiu、ならびに -kosanu 派生形における mai、nai、ser はすべて擬声語根である。"},"type":"membership","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["hum","kit","pat","put","rim","shiu","mai","nai","ser"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0126-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--aspectual-suffixes-attach-to-mimetics","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--ideophones"],"statement":{"en":"Certain repetitive and aspectual suffixes frequently attach to onomatopoeic and mimetic roots.","ja":"特定の反復・アスペクト接尾辞は、擬声語・擬態語の語根に高頻度で後接する。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"major","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-natara","-hitara","-itara","-rototke","-rototo","-atki","-tektek"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0204-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--ideophone-kiriri-oar-creak","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--ideophones"],"statement":{"en":"The onomatopoeic word kiriri represents the creaking sound of rowing an oar.","ja":"擬声語 kiriri は櫓を漕ぐときのきしむ音を表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["kiriri"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0535-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--etymology-sekor-saying-quotative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--ideophones"],"statement":{"en":"The quotative particle sekór can be analyzed etymologically as se-kor 'saying', containing a root se 'to say, do' found in compound ideophones.","ja":"引用副詞 sekór の語源は se-kor「と言いながら」と解釈でき、複合擬声・擬態語に見られる「と言う・とする」の se を含む。"},"type":"diachrony","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"tentative","conditions":[]},"forms":["sekór","se","kor"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:tamura1972@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0004-07","stance":"proposes"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--sakhalin-interjection-aii-pain","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, 'a'ii is an interjection used to express pain.","ja":"樺太アイヌにおいて、'a'ii は苦痛を訴える際に用いられる間投詞である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["'a'ii"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0116-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--sakhalin-interjection-hee-gender-neutral","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, the interjection hee is used by both men and women to express mild surprise.","ja":"樺太アイヌにおいて、間投詞 hee は男女ともに用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["hee"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0116-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
