{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--chiri-interjection-inventory-size","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Chiri (1936) documents approximately fifty interjections in Ainu.","ja":"知里（1936）は約50語のアイヌ語感動詞を記載している。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0124-05","stance":"reports"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0125-07","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--shizunai-interjection-ayay-pain","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai, ayay is an interjection expressing pain ('ouch').","ja":"静内方言において、ayay は苦痛（「痛い」）を表す感動詞である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ayay"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0126-01","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0127-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--shizunai-interjection-ononno-gratitude","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"In Shizunai, ononno is an interjection expressing happiness and gratitude.","ja":"静内方言において、ononno は喜びや感謝を表す感動詞である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["ononno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0126-02","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0127-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contrasts","claim":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--interjection-ononno-triumph","differs_in":"dialect","note":"Refsing describes ononno in Shizunai as expressing happiness and gratitude, whereas Kindaichi & Chiri gloss it as praise or triumph ('hurrah')."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--shizunai-pakno-pakno-interjection-use","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"Used alone, pakno can function as an interjection, pakno pakno 'enough! enough!'.","ja":"単独で用いられる場合、pakno は間投詞 pakno pakno「もう十分だ！」として機能しうる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["pakno","pakno pakno"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0160-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0161-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--saru-interjection-hesto-hesto","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--inventory"],"statement":{"en":"In Saru, the expression hesto hesto means 'there, didn't I tell you? / see?'.","ja":"沙流方言において、hesto hesto は「そら見たことか」を意味する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/saru"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["hesto hesto"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0316-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--verb-forming-suffix-se-phenomimetic","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--morphosyntax"],"statement":{"en":"The verbalizing suffix -se forms phenomimetic (ideophonic) verbs as well as phonomimetic ones.","ja":"動詞形成接尾辞 -se は、擬声語だけでなく擬態語（擬容語）の動詞も形成する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"major","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-se"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0133-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--verb-forming-suffix-ke-mimetics","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--morphosyntax"],"statement":{"en":"Like -se, the verbalizing suffix -ke forms onomatopoeic and phenomimetic verbs.","ja":"-se と同様に、動詞形成接尾辞 -ke は擬声語および擬態語（擬容語）の動詞を形成する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"major","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-ke"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0134-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--exclamatory-suffix-po-in-interjections","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--morphosyntax"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -po functions as an exclamatory element in interjections such as ayapo!, oyoyo(po)!, and wakkapo!.","ja":"接尾辞 -po は、ayapo!、oyoyo(po)!、wakkapo! などの間投詞において感嘆接尾辞として現れる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"specific","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-po","ayapo","oyoyo","wakkapo"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0182-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--interjections-constitute-independent-clauses-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--morphosyntax"],"statement":{"en":"Interjections constitute independent sentences on their own and enter into no grammatical relations with other elements.","ja":"間投詞は単独で独立した文を構成し、他のいかなる統語要素とも文法的関係を結ばない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0287-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--interjections-can-integrate-into-sentences","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--morphosyntax"],"statement":{"en":"Interjections may either stand as isolated exclamations or initiate or occasionally be interpolated into larger full sentences.","ja":"感動詞は孤立した感嘆文をなすほか、完全な文の文頭に立つことや文中に挿入されることもある。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0125-05","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[{"kind":"contradicts","claim":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--interjections-constitute-independent-clauses-only","differs_in":"framework","note":"Nakagawa claims interjections never enter grammatical relations with other elements, while Refsing observes them initiating or interpolating into full sentences."}],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--sakhalin-interjection-definition-standalone-sentence","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--overview"],"statement":{"en":"In Sakhalin Ainu, interjections are defined as words whose internal grammatical structure is unclear but which constitute an entire sentence by themselves.","ja":"樺太アイヌにおいて、間投詞は文法的構造は不明だが単独で一文を構成する語として定義される。"},"type":"terminology","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:sakhalin"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:murasaki2025@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0116-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--interjections-carry-inherent-modality","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Interjections inherently carry modality such that a word forms a fully terminated sentence after which nothing can follow.","ja":"間投詞はそれ自体にモダリティを帯びており、単語単体で完全な終結文を成すため、後続要素をとることができない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["irayapka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0401-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--functional-range-of-interjections","revision":1,"topic":"topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topics":["topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism","topic:discourse/interjections-ideophones-sound-symbolism--overview"],"statement":{"en":"Interjections function to call attention to the speaker, to respond to conversational turns and transactions, or to express emotional reactions.","ja":"感動詞の機能は、注意喚起、社会的やり取りへの応答、あるいは感情的反応の表出である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"universal","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":[],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0124-04","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0125-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
